<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 7 August, from 461 to 1998.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">461 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,565 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Western Emperor Majorian is executed on Ricimer's orders</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Majorian, the last Western emperor to attempt a real recovery of the empire, was arrested and beheaded by his general Ricimer. Afterwards Ricimer ruled through puppet emperors.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-washington.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1782 CE <span class="tih-ago">244 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Washington creates the Badge of Military Merit</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Washington established a purple cloth heart to honour enlisted soldiers for meritorious action. Revived in 1932 as the Purple Heart, it is now awarded to those wounded or killed in US service.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1819 CE <span class="tih-ago">207 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Simón Bolívar wins the Battle of Boyacá</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a daring march over the Andes, Bolívar's army defeated the royalists at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boyaca-department">Boyacá</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a> fell days later, securing the independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a>, present-day Colombia.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1942 CE <span class="tih-ago">84 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Marines land on Guadalcanal</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">US Marines landed on Guadalcanal in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> Islands, the first major American offensive of the Pacific war. Six months of fighting ended in a Japanese withdrawal.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1947 CE <span class="tih-ago">79 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Thor Heyerdahl's Kon-Tiki raft reaches Polynesia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After 101 days and some 7,000 km from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thor">Thor</a> Heyerdahl's balsa raft ran onto the reef at Raroia. The voyage showed that prehistoric people could have crossed the Pacific on such craft.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1998 CE <span class="tih-ago">28 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Al-Qaeda bombs US embassies in Kenya and Tanzania</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Truck bombs exploded almost simultaneously at the US embassies in Nairobi and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dar-es-salaam">Dar es Salaam</a>, killing 224 people, most of them Africans. The attacks brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osama-bin-laden">Osama bin Laden</a> to world attention.</p></div></li></ol>
